# Defect 510's qualified spelling (lane b16-compiler, 2026-10-09): a constant
# of another module holding a function, called by its qualified name,
# `helper.DOUBLE(4)`. The checker's qualified arm answered the error type with
# no diagnostic, and the build stopped at exit 2, *monomorphisation produced
# an ill-formed program*; the call now reads the constant and calls what it
# holds, as `f = helper.DOUBLE` then `f(4)` always did.
use helper

function main()
    print(helper.DOUBLE(4))
    print(helper.DOUBLE(helper.LIMIT) + 1)
